{
  "_meaning": "Which directories hold each specification app's own source. This decides what counts as evidence for that app, so it is recorded with reasons rather than derived from directory-name guessing.",
  "_measured_on": "2026-10-31",
  "_measured_at_source": "254e1f2b",
  "_root_classes": {
    "app-local": "the app's own workspace directory, excluding its DonorMirror corpus (that is indexed as 'mirror')",
    "shared": "9to1 Workspace/shared/src plus native: the shared implementation the specification requires every app to use (one implementation per app, Home Core service plane)",
    "tests": "9to1 Workspace/shared/tests plus framework/*/Tests: genuine test projects, including the Haven.Desktop.Tests and Haven.Core.Tests suites",
    "framework": "framework/: the CUI language, compiler and runtime plus the donor-derived Avalonia fork",
    "models": "9to1 Models/: Dulche model packages and the pinned native inference engines",
    "workspace-other": "other 9to1 Workspace app directories, used only for cross-cutting requirements that genuinely span apps"
  },
  "_notes": [
    "Measured 31 Oct 2026: 'shared' holds 2,956 first-party source files while the app directories hold far fewer (Build 0 own .cui/.cs outside donor trees, Connect 0, Planner 0). Treating only app-local directories as evidence would report Build as empty when its scope lives in Dev/Sites/Stacks and shared/src.",
    "Build combines Dev + Sites + Stacks per the specification's one-app rule, so all three are Build's app-local roots; the separate 'Build' directory is included too.",
    "Connect is scoped to email by the owner, and Mail is its email mode, so Connect's app-local roots are Connect + Mail; non-mail Connect surfaces stay visible because the register keeps the full denominator.",
    "Automations, Voice & Vision and Dulche have no workspace directory of their own: measured, their implementation lives in shared/src and their tests in shared/tests, so they get shared + tests + models roots and no app-local claim.",
    "CUI requirements are framework-conformance requirements, so their roots are framework/ (not an app directory).",
    "Every DonorMirror corpus is reclassified as 'mirror' during indexing: a Stage A donor mirror is structure without specification behaviour and must never raise an app's code-presence tier.",
    "Corrected 31 Oct 2026 after a measured implausibility: Games reported 72% test-asserted and Play 70% while neither app exists in this repository, because their recorded roots were the whole '9to1 Workspace'. No app is scored against the whole workspace, and an app with no first-party source gets no roots so its requirements land in NO-EVIDENCE.",
    "Markdown excluded from the evidence corpus after the first hand audit measured 6 of 12 credited rows as false, four of them app gap-manifest documents crediting a recorded absence as if it were an implementation. docs/specification is not a root for any app.",
    "eng/ is a root only for 'packaging' (its requirements are genuinely about the build and launch tooling) and not for other apps: measured, treating eng/ as a product root credited a 9to1 OS requirement from donor-registry metadata. Apps with no product source get no roots and therefore measure zero evidence."
  ],
